{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790260661829,"sessionID":"ses_f2c26c33fffebSfWZ9ZBPjdC7e","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_9d460a228e91466084b52bc2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/task_config.json"},"output":"<path>/workspace/task_config.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"instruction\": \"Finish the Explosion hierarchy so the ArcingChunks emitter works as wanted: set ArcingChunks to one_shot, lifetime 3s, randomness about 0.7, give it a QuadMesh draw pass and a StandardMaterial3D billboard with bright emission, and drive it with a ParticleProcessMaterial that fires from the default spread at 8\\u201312 m/s, enables rigid collision with bounce 1.0, uses collision_use_scale, and sets a constant sub emitter frequency of 100 Hz with the sub_emitter path pointing to ../ArcingChunkSmoke. Add the GPUParticlesCollisionBox3D named ArcingChunkCollision, positioned just below the emitter and scaled to 40\\u00d71\\u00d740 so debris collides as shown in the collision segment of the video. Configure ArcingChunkSmoke to emit ~1000 particles with a ShaderMaterial referencing res://assets/shaders/SmokeShader.gdshader (NoiseTexture = res://assets/shaders/NoiseResource.tres) and a ParticleProcessMaterial that rotates sprites, uses the warm gradient/curve combo from the repo, lifetime 3 s, gravity (0,1,0), linear accel ~2, scale curve peaks between 8 and 15, and turbulence influence about 0.005\\u20130.01 so the smoke puffs appear along the chunk trails.\"\n3: }\n\n(End of file - total 3 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"instruction\": \"Finish the Explosion hierarchy so the ArcingChunks emitter works as wanted: set ArcingChunks to one_shot, lifetime 3s, randomness about 0.7, give it a QuadMesh draw pass and a StandardMaterial3D billboard with bright emission, and drive it with a ParticleProcessMaterial that fires from the default spread at 8\\u201312 m/s, enables rigid collision with bounce 1.0, uses